{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want a streaming chat in your app. TanStack AI streams from a server route. The hook for your framework renders the tokens."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a React + Start app with BYOK, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/basic-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Chat"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For an MCP server with a tool, a resource, and a prompt, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/mcp-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build an MCP Server"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For an image from a prompt, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/generate-image","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generate Image"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a table that fills as JSON streams, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/streaming-structured-table","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming Structured Table"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a blog desk where a researcher and an SEO agent run together and a writer uses their notes, open "},{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/subagents","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subagents"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"tip","title":"Tip","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you do not want a key per provider, "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openrouter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" gives you 300+ models with one API key."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native or Expo needs an absolute server URL and an XHR transport. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./quick-start-react-native","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start: React Native"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No UI: see "},{"type":"link","href":"./quick-start-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start: Server Only"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-react\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-vue\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-solid\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-svelte\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-preact\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-angular\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-client\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-octane\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\",\"octane\"]],\"remix\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-remix\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\",\"remix\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-stream-from-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Stream from the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". Then wrap the result with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This works with TanStack Start, Next.js, SvelteKit, Hono, and any host that returns a Web "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Remix controller action can return this same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If your server is Node streams (Express), see "},{"type":"link","href":"./quick-start-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start: Server Only"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Put the API key on the server:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" at runtime. Do not send this key to the browser."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you do not want a server key, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-render-the-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Render the chat"}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework","attributes":{},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"react"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":". Hold the composer text in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useState"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" updates as chunks arrive. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" while the run is in flight."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"vue"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vue"},{"type":"text","value":". If you are in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<script setup>"},{"type":"text","value":", read refs with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":". The template unwraps them."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\n\nconst input = ref('')\n\nconst { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\n\nfunction handleSubmit() {\n  if (input.value.trim() && !isLoading.value) {\n    sendMessage(input.value)\n    input.value = ''\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <div v-for=\"message in messages\" :key=\"message.id\">\n      <template v-for=\"(part, index) in message.parts\" :key=\"index\">\n        <p v-if=\"part.type === 'text'\">{{ part.content }}</p>\n      </template>\n    </div>\n    <form @submit.prevent=\"handleSubmit\">\n      <input v-model=\"input\" :disabled=\"isLoading\" />\n      <button v-if=\"isLoading\" type=\"button\" @click=\"stop\">Stop</button>\n      <button v-else type=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!input.trim()\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n  </div>\n</template>","lang":"vue"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The composable stops in-flight requests when the component unmounts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-vue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"solid"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-solid"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":" are accessors. Call them as functions."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { For, createSignal } from \"solid-js\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-solid\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = createSignal(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <For each={messages()}>\n        {(message) => (\n          <div>\n            <For each={message.parts}>\n              {(part) =>\n                part.type === \"text\" ? <p>{part.content}</p> : null\n              }\n            </For>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input().trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input());\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input()}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading() ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-solid","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"svelte"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-svelte"},{"type":"text","value":". The return object uses reactive getters. Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.messages"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":" with no extra wrapper."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\nlet input = $state('')\n\nconst chat = createChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\n\nfunction handleSubmit() {\n  if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\n    chat.sendMessage(input)\n    input = ''\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    <div>\n      {#each message.parts as part}\n        {#if part.type === 'text'}\n          <p>{part.content}</p>\n        {/if}\n      {/each}\n    </div>\n  {/each}\n\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n    {#if chat.isLoading}\n      <button type=\"button\" onclick={() => chat.stop()}>Stop</button>\n    {:else}\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!input.trim()}>Send</button>\n    {/if}\n  </form>\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the component can unmount while a response streams, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onDestroy"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-svelte","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Svelte API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"preact"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-preact"},{"type":"text","value":". Hold the composer text with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useState"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preact/hooks"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"preact/hooks\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-preact\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-preact","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Preact API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"angular"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectChat"},{"type":"text","value":" in a field initializer. State is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Signal"},{"type":"text","value":". Read it by calling the function."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from \"@angular/core\";\nimport { FormsModule } from \"@angular/forms\";\nimport { injectChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-angular\";\n\n@Component({\n  selector: \"app-chat\",\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [FormsModule],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      @for (message of chat.messages(); track message.id) {\n        <div>\n          @for (part of message.parts; track $index) {\n            @if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              <p>{{ part.content }}</p>\n            }\n          }\n        </div>\n      }\n      <form (submit)=\"send($event)\">\n        <input [(ngModel)]=\"draft\" name=\"draft\" [disabled]=\"chat.isLoading()\" />\n        @if (chat.isLoading()) {\n          <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"chat.stop()\">Stop</button>\n        } @else {\n          <button type=\"submit\" [disabled]=\"!draft.trim()\">Send</button>\n        }\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class ChatComponent {\n  chat = injectChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  draft = \"\";\n\n  send(event: Event) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    const text = this.draft.trim();\n    if (text && !this.chat.isLoading()) {\n      void this.chat.sendMessage(text);\n      this.draft = \"\";\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectChat"},{"type":"text","value":" in a field initializer or the constructor. A call in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ngOnInit"},{"type":"text","value":" throws."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectChat"},{"type":"text","value":" subscribes to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DestroyRef"},{"type":"text","value":". In-flight requests stop when the component is destroyed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-angular","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"octane"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-octane"},{"type":"text","value":". Hold the composer text in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useState"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"octane"},{"type":"text","value":". Octane text controls fire "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInput"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-octane"},{"type":"text","value":" publishes uncompiled "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".tsrx"},{"type":"text","value":" source. Add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"octane/compiler/vite"},{"type":"text","value":" (or the rspack / rspeedy equivalent) to the app build."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"octane\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-octane\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          <p>\n            {message.parts\n              .filter((part) => part.type === \"text\")\n              .map((part) => part.content)\n              .join(\"\")}\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          void sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          disabled={isLoading}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The hook calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"},{"type":"text","value":" on mount. It calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detach()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dispose()"},{"type":"text","value":" on unmount."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-octane","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Octane API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"framework-panel","tagName":"md-framework-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-framework":"remix"},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChat(handle, options)"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-remix"},{"type":"text","value":" inside a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientEntry"},{"type":"text","value":" island. Put "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" in setup. They are not serializable "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientEntry"},{"type":"text","value":" props."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-remix"},{"type":"text","value":" publishes uncompiled source. Remix compiles JSX through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"jsxImportSource"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"remix/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". Bind the form with the Remix "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"on"},{"type":"text","value":" mixin."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-remix\";\nimport { clientEntry, on, type Handle } from \"remix/ui\";\n\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function Chat(handle: Handle) {\n    const chat = createChat(handle, {\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    });\n\n    return () => (\n      <div>\n        {chat.messages.map((message) => (\n          <div key={message.id}>\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n              part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n            )}\n          </div>\n        ))}\n        <form\n          mix={on(\"submit\", (event) => {\n            event.preventDefault();\n            const form = event.currentTarget;\n            const text = String(\n              new FormData(form).get(\"message\") ?? \"\",\n            ).trim();\n            if (text === \"\") {\n              return;\n            }\n            form.reset();\n            void chat.sendMessage(text);\n          })}\n        >\n          <input name=\"message\" disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n          {chat.isLoading ? (\n            <button type=\"button\" mix={on(\"click\", () => chat.stop())}>\n              Stop\n            </button>\n          ) : (\n            <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n          )}\n        </form>\n      </div>\n    );\n  },\n);","lang":"tsx","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.messages"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat.isLoading"},{"type":"text","value":" in the render function so each paint sees the latest values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../api/ai-remix","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remix API"}]},{"type":"text","value":". For a typed headless chat UI, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../ui/remix","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remix Chat UI"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}],"properties":{"data-available-frameworks":"[\"react\",\"vue\",\"solid\",\"svelte\",\"preact\",\"angular\",\"octane\",\"remix\"]","data-framework-meta":"{\"codeBlocksByFramework\":{\"react\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useState } from \\\"react\\\";\\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \\\"@tanstack/ai-react\\\";\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\\\"\\\");\\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\\\"/api/chat\\\"),\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <>\\n      {messages.map((message) => (\\n        <div key={message.id}>\\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\\n            part.type === \\\"text\\\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\\n          )}\\n        </div>\\n      ))}\\n      <form\\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\\n          event.preventDefault();\\n          if (input.trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n            return;\\n          }\\n          sendMessage(input);\\n          setInput(\\\"\\\");\\n        }}\\n      >\\n        <input\\n          value={input}\\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\\n        />\\n        {isLoading ? (\\n          <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={stop}>\\n            Stop\\n          </button>\\n        ) : (\\n          <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send</button>\\n        )}\\n      </form>\\n    </>\\n  );\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"vue\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"<script setup lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\\n\\nconst input = ref('')\\n\\nconst { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n})\\n\\nfunction handleSubmit() {\\n  if (input.value.trim() && !isLoading.value) {\\n    sendMessage(input.value)\\n    input.value = ''\\n  }\\n}\\n</script>\\n\\n<template>\\n  <div>\\n    <div v-for=\\\"message in messages\\\" :key=\\\"message.id\\\">\\n      <template v-for=\\\"(part, index) in message.parts\\\" :key=\\\"index\\\">\\n        <p v-if=\\\"part.type === 'text'\\\">{{ part.content }}</p>\\n      </template>\\n    </div>\\n    <form @submit.prevent=\\\"handleSubmit\\\">\\n      <input v-model=\\\"input\\\" :disabled=\\\"isLoading\\\" />\\n      <button v-if=\\\"isLoading\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" @click=\\\"stop\\\">Stop</button>\\n      <button v-else type=\\\"submit\\\" :disabled=\\\"!input.trim()\\\">Send</button>\\n    </form>\\n  </div>\\n</template>\",\"language\":\"vue\"}],\"solid\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { For, createSignal } from \\\"solid-js\\\";\\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \\\"@tanstack/ai-solid\\\";\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const [input, setInput] = createSignal(\\\"\\\");\\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\\\"/api/chat\\\"),\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <>\\n      <For each={messages()}>\\n        {(message) => (\\n          <div>\\n            <For each={message.parts}>\\n              {(part) =>\\n                part.type === \\\"text\\\" ? <p>{part.content}</p> : null\\n              }\\n            </For>\\n          </div>\\n        )}\\n      </For>\\n      <form\\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\\n          event.preventDefault();\\n          if (input().trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n            return;\\n          }\\n          sendMessage(input());\\n          setInput(\\\"\\\");\\n        }}\\n      >\\n        <input\\n          value={input()}\\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\\n        />\\n        {isLoading() ? (\\n          <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={stop}>\\n            Stop\\n          </button>\\n        ) : (\\n          <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send</button>\\n        )}\\n      </form>\\n    </>\\n  );\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"svelte\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"<script lang=\\\"ts\\\">\\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\\n\\nlet input = $state('')\\n\\nconst chat = createChat({\\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\\n})\\n\\nfunction handleSubmit() {\\n  if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\\n    chat.sendMessage(input)\\n    input = ''\\n  }\\n}\\n</script>\\n\\n<div>\\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\\n    <div>\\n      {#each message.parts as part}\\n        {#if part.type === 'text'}\\n          <p>{part.content}</p>\\n        {/if}\\n      {/each}\\n    </div>\\n  {/each}\\n\\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\\n    {#if chat.isLoading}\\n      <button type=\\\"button\\\" onclick={() => chat.stop()}>Stop</button>\\n    {:else}\\n      <button type=\\\"submit\\\" disabled={!input.trim()}>Send</button>\\n    {/if}\\n  </form>\\n</div>\",\"language\":\"svelte\"}],\"preact\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useState } from \\\"preact/hooks\\\";\\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \\\"@tanstack/ai-preact\\\";\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\\\"\\\");\\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\\\"/api/chat\\\"),\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <>\\n      {messages.map((message) => (\\n        <div key={message.id}>\\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\\n            part.type === \\\"text\\\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\\n          )}\\n        </div>\\n      ))}\\n      <form\\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\\n          event.preventDefault();\\n          if (input.trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n            return;\\n          }\\n          sendMessage(input);\\n          setInput(\\\"\\\");\\n        }}\\n      >\\n        <input\\n          value={input}\\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\\n        />\\n        {isLoading ? (\\n          <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={stop}>\\n            Stop\\n          </button>\\n        ) : (\\n          <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send</button>\\n        )}\\n      </form>\\n    </>\\n  );\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"angular\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { Component } from \\\"@angular/core\\\";\\nimport { FormsModule } from \\\"@angular/forms\\\";\\nimport { injectChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \\\"@tanstack/ai-angular\\\";\\n\\n@Component({\\n  selector: \\\"app-chat\\\",\\n  standalone: true,\\n  imports: [FormsModule],\\n  template: `\\n    <div>\\n      @for (message of chat.messages(); track message.id) {\\n        <div>\\n          @for (part of message.parts; track $index) {\\n            @if (part.type === \\\"text\\\") {\\n              <p>{{ part.content }}</p>\\n            }\\n          }\\n        </div>\\n      }\\n      <form (submit)=\\\"send($event)\\\">\\n        <input [(ngModel)]=\\\"draft\\\" name=\\\"draft\\\" [disabled]=\\\"chat.isLoading()\\\" />\\n        @if (chat.isLoading()) {\\n          <button type=\\\"button\\\" (click)=\\\"chat.stop()\\\">Stop</button>\\n        } @else {\\n          <button type=\\\"submit\\\" [disabled]=\\\"!draft.trim()\\\">Send</button>\\n        }\\n      </form>\\n    </div>\\n  `,\\n})\\nexport class ChatComponent {\\n  chat = injectChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\\\"/api/chat\\\"),\\n  });\\n\\n  draft = \\\"\\\";\\n\\n  send(event: Event) {\\n    event.preventDefault();\\n    const text = this.draft.trim();\\n    if (text && !this.chat.isLoading()) {\\n      void this.chat.sendMessage(text);\\n      this.draft = \\\"\\\";\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\",\"language\":\"typescript\"}],\"octane\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { useState } from \\\"octane\\\";\\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \\\"@tanstack/ai-octane\\\";\\n\\nexport function Chat() {\\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\\\"\\\");\\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\\\"/api/chat\\\"),\\n  });\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div>\\n      {messages.map((message) => (\\n        <div key={message.id}>\\n          <p>\\n            {message.parts\\n              .filter((part) => part.type === \\\"text\\\")\\n              .map((part) => part.content)\\n              .join(\\\"\\\")}\\n          </p>\\n        </div>\\n      ))}\\n      <form\\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\\n          event.preventDefault();\\n          if (input.trim() === \\\"\\\") {\\n            return;\\n          }\\n          void sendMessage(input);\\n          setInput(\\\"\\\");\\n        }}\\n      >\\n        <input\\n          value={input}\\n          disabled={isLoading}\\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\\n        />\\n        {isLoading ? (\\n          <button type=\\\"button\\\" onClick={stop}>\\n            Stop\\n          </button>\\n        ) : (\\n          <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send</button>\\n        )}\\n      </form>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n}\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}],\"remix\":[{\"title\":\"\",\"code\":\"import { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \\\"@tanstack/ai-remix\\\";\\nimport { clientEntry, on, type Handle } from \\\"remix/ui\\\";\\n\\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(\\n  import.meta.url,\\n  function Chat(handle: Handle) {\\n    const chat = createChat(handle, {\\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\\\"/api/chat\\\"),\\n    });\\n\\n    return () => (\\n      <div>\\n        {chat.messages.map((message) => (\\n          <div key={message.id}>\\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\\n              part.type === \\\"text\\\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\\n            )}\\n          </div>\\n        ))}\\n        <form\\n          mix={on(\\\"submit\\\", (event) => {\\n            event.preventDefault();\\n            const form = event.currentTarget;\\n            const text = String(\\n              new FormData(form).get(\\\"message\\\") ?? \\\"\\\",\\n            ).trim();\\n            if (text === \\\"\\\") {\\n              return;\\n            }\\n            form.reset();\\n            void chat.sendMessage(text);\\n          })}\\n        >\\n          <input name=\\\"message\\\" disabled={chat.isLoading} />\\n          {chat.isLoading ? (\\n            <button type=\\\"button\\\" mix={on(\\\"click\\\", () => chat.stop())}>\\n              Stop\\n            </button>\\n          ) : (\\n            <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send</button>\\n          )}\\n        </form>\\n      </div>\\n    );\\n  },\\n);\",\"language\":\"tsx\"}]}}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Send a message. Tokens show up in the UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"later","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Later"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tools/tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for function calling"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../chat/streaming","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for cancel, callbacks, and transports"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for other providers"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-install","text":"1. Install","level":2},{"id":"2-stream-from-the-server","text":"2. Stream from the server","level":2},{"id":"3-render-the-chat","text":"3. Render the chat","level":2},{"id":"later","text":"Later","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","octane","remix","vanilla"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou want a streaming chat in your app. TanStack AI streams from a server route. The hook for your framework renders the tokens.\n\nFor a React + Start app with BYOK, open [Basic Chat](../tutorials/basic-chat).\n\nFor an MCP server with a tool, a resource, and a prompt, open [Build an MCP Server](../tutorials/mcp-server).\n\nFor an image from a prompt, open [Generate Image](../tutorials/generate-image).\n\nFor a table that fills as JSON streams, open [Streaming Structured Table](../tutorials/streaming-structured-table).\n\nFor a blog desk where a researcher and an SEO agent run together and a writer uses their notes, open [Subagents](../tutorials/subagents).\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If you do not want a key per provider, [OpenRouter](../adapters/openrouter) gives you 300+ models with one API key.\n\nReact Native or Expo needs an absolute server URL and an XHR transport. See [Quick Start: React Native](./quick-start-react-native).\n\nNo UI: see [Quick Start: Server Only](./quick-start-server).\n\n## 1. Install\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openai\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-vue @tanstack/ai-openai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-solid @tanstack/ai-openai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-svelte @tanstack/ai-openai\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-preact @tanstack/ai-openai\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-angular @tanstack/ai-openai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client @tanstack/ai-openai\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-octane @tanstack/ai-openai octane\nremix: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-remix @tanstack/ai-openai remix\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## 2. Stream from the server\n\nCall `chat()`. Then wrap the result with `toServerSentEventsResponse`.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nThis works with TanStack Start, Next.js, SvelteKit, Hono, and any host that returns a Web `Response`.\n\nA Remix controller action can return this same `Response`.\n\nIf your server is Node streams (Express), see [Quick Start: Server Only](./quick-start-server).\n\nPut the API key on the server:\n\n```bash\nOPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key\n```\n\nThe adapter reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` at runtime. Do not send this key to the browser.\n\nIf you do not want a server key, see [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## 3. Render the chat\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-react`. Hold the composer text in `useState`. Pass it to `sendMessage`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`messages` updates as chunks arrive. `isLoading` is `true` while the run is in flight.\n\nSee the [React API](../api/ai-react).\n\n# Vue\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-vue`. If you are in `<script setup>`, read refs with `.value`. The template unwraps them.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\n\nconst input = ref('')\n\nconst { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\n\nfunction handleSubmit() {\n  if (input.value.trim() && !isLoading.value) {\n    sendMessage(input.value)\n    input.value = ''\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <div v-for=\"message in messages\" :key=\"message.id\">\n      <template v-for=\"(part, index) in message.parts\" :key=\"index\">\n        <p v-if=\"part.type === 'text'\">{{ part.content }}</p>\n      </template>\n    </div>\n    <form @submit.prevent=\"handleSubmit\">\n      <input v-model=\"input\" :disabled=\"isLoading\" />\n      <button v-if=\"isLoading\" type=\"button\" @click=\"stop\">Stop</button>\n      <button v-else type=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!input.trim()\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\nThe composable stops in-flight requests when the component unmounts.\n\nSee the [Vue API](../api/ai-vue).\n\n# Solid\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-solid`. `messages` and `isLoading` are accessors. Call them as functions.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { For, createSignal } from \"solid-js\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-solid\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = createSignal(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <For each={messages()}>\n        {(message) => (\n          <div>\n            <For each={message.parts}>\n              {(part) =>\n                part.type === \"text\" ? <p>{part.content}</p> : null\n              }\n            </For>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input().trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input());\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input()}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading() ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nSee the [Solid API](../api/ai-solid).\n\n# Svelte\n\nCall `createChat` from `@tanstack/ai-svelte`. The return object uses reactive getters. Read `chat.messages` and `chat.isLoading` with no extra wrapper.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\nlet input = $state('')\n\nconst chat = createChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\n\nfunction handleSubmit() {\n  if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\n    chat.sendMessage(input)\n    input = ''\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    <div>\n      {#each message.parts as part}\n        {#if part.type === 'text'}\n          <p>{part.content}</p>\n        {/if}\n      {/each}\n    </div>\n  {/each}\n\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n    {#if chat.isLoading}\n      <button type=\"button\" onclick={() => chat.stop()}>Stop</button>\n    {:else}\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!input.trim()}>Send</button>\n    {/if}\n  </form>\n</div>\n```\n\nIf the component can unmount while a response streams, call `chat.stop()` in `onDestroy`.\n\nSee the [Svelte API](../api/ai-svelte).\n\n# Preact\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-preact`. Hold the composer text with `useState` from `preact/hooks`.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from \"preact/hooks\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-preact\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nSee the [Preact API](../api/ai-preact).\n\n# Angular\n\nCall `injectChat` in a field initializer. State is a `Signal`. Read it by calling the function.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { Component } from \"@angular/core\";\nimport { FormsModule } from \"@angular/forms\";\nimport { injectChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-angular\";\n\n@Component({\n  selector: \"app-chat\",\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [FormsModule],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      @for (message of chat.messages(); track message.id) {\n        <div>\n          @for (part of message.parts; track $index) {\n            @if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              <p>{{ part.content }}</p>\n            }\n          }\n        </div>\n      }\n      <form (submit)=\"send($event)\">\n        <input [(ngModel)]=\"draft\" name=\"draft\" [disabled]=\"chat.isLoading()\" />\n        @if (chat.isLoading()) {\n          <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"chat.stop()\">Stop</button>\n        } @else {\n          <button type=\"submit\" [disabled]=\"!draft.trim()\">Send</button>\n        }\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class ChatComponent {\n  chat = injectChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  draft = \"\";\n\n  send(event: Event) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    const text = this.draft.trim();\n    if (text && !this.chat.isLoading()) {\n      void this.chat.sendMessage(text);\n      this.draft = \"\";\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCall `injectChat` in a field initializer or the constructor. A call in `ngOnInit` throws.\n\n`injectChat` subscribes to `DestroyRef`. In-flight requests stop when the component is destroyed.\n\nSee the [Angular API](../api/ai-angular).\n\n# Octane\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-octane`. Hold the composer text in `useState` from `octane`. Octane text controls fire `onInput`.\n\n`@tanstack/ai-octane` publishes uncompiled `.tsrx` source. Add `octane/compiler/vite` (or the rspack / rspeedy equivalent) to the app build.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from \"octane\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-octane\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          <p>\n            {message.parts\n              .filter((part) => part.type === \"text\")\n              .map((part) => part.content)\n              .join(\"\")}\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          void sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          disabled={isLoading}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe hook calls `attach()` on mount. It calls `detach()` and `dispose()` on unmount.\n\nSee the [Octane API](../api/ai-octane).\n\n# Remix\n\nCall `createChat(handle, options)` from `@tanstack/ai-remix` inside a `clientEntry` island. Put `connection` and `tools` in setup. They are not serializable `clientEntry` props.\n\n`@tanstack/ai-remix` publishes uncompiled source. Remix compiles JSX through `jsxImportSource` `remix/ui`. Bind the form with the Remix `on` mixin.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-remix\";\nimport { clientEntry, on, type Handle } from \"remix/ui\";\n\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function Chat(handle: Handle) {\n    const chat = createChat(handle, {\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    });\n\n    return () => (\n      <div>\n        {chat.messages.map((message) => (\n          <div key={message.id}>\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n              part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n            )}\n          </div>\n        ))}\n        <form\n          mix={on(\"submit\", (event) => {\n            event.preventDefault();\n            const form = event.currentTarget;\n            const text = String(\n              new FormData(form).get(\"message\") ?? \"\",\n            ).trim();\n            if (text === \"\") {\n              return;\n            }\n            form.reset();\n            void chat.sendMessage(text);\n          })}\n        >\n          <input name=\"message\" disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n          {chat.isLoading ? (\n            <button type=\"button\" mix={on(\"click\", () => chat.stop())}>\n              Stop\n            </button>\n          ) : (\n            <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n          )}\n        </form>\n      </div>\n    );\n  },\n);\n```\n\nRead `chat.messages` and `chat.isLoading` in the render function so each paint sees the latest values.\n\nSee the [Remix API](../api/ai-remix). For a typed headless chat UI, see [Remix Chat UI](../ui/remix).\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nSend a message. Tokens show up in the UI.\n\n## Later\n\n- [Tools](../tools/tools) for function calling\n- [Streaming](../chat/streaming) for cancel, callbacks, and transports\n- [Adapters](../adapters/openai) for other providers\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\nid: quick-start\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Add a streaming TanStack AI chat to your app. Pick a framework, install, stream from a server route, and render with the matching hook.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - quick start\n  - useChat\n  - injectChat\n  - createChat\n  - streaming chat\n  - openai\n  - react\n  - vue\n  - solid\n  - svelte\n  - preact\n  - angular\n  - octane\n  - remix\nredirect_from:\n  - /getting-started/quick-start-vue\n  - /getting-started/quick-start-svelte\n  - /getting-started/quick-start-angular\n  - /getting-started/quick-start-octane\n---\n\nYou want a streaming chat in your app. TanStack AI streams from a server route. The hook for your framework renders the tokens.\n\nFor a React + Start app with BYOK, open [Basic Chat](../tutorials/basic-chat).\n\nFor an MCP server with a tool, a resource, and a prompt, open [Build an MCP Server](../tutorials/mcp-server).\n\nFor an image from a prompt, open [Generate Image](../tutorials/generate-image).\n\nFor a table that fills as JSON streams, open [Streaming Structured Table](../tutorials/streaming-structured-table).\n\nFor a blog desk where a researcher and an SEO agent run together and a writer uses their notes, open [Subagents](../tutorials/subagents).\n\n> [!TIP]\n> If you do not want a key per provider, [OpenRouter](../adapters/openrouter) gives you 300+ models with one API key.\n\nReact Native or Expo needs an absolute server URL and an XHR transport. See [Quick Start: React Native](./quick-start-react-native).\n\nNo UI: see [Quick Start: Server Only](./quick-start-server).\n\n## 1. Install\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openai\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-vue @tanstack/ai-openai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-solid @tanstack/ai-openai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-svelte @tanstack/ai-openai\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-preact @tanstack/ai-openai\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-angular @tanstack/ai-openai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-client @tanstack/ai-openai\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-octane @tanstack/ai-openai octane\nremix: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-remix @tanstack/ai-openai remix\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## 2. Stream from the server\n\nCall `chat()`. Then wrap the result with `toServerSentEventsResponse`.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, threadId, runId } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.6\"),\n    messages,\n    threadId,\n    runId,\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nThis works with TanStack Start, Next.js, SvelteKit, Hono, and any host that returns a Web `Response`.\n\nA Remix controller action can return this same `Response`.\n\nIf your server is Node streams (Express), see [Quick Start: Server Only](./quick-start-server).\n\nPut the API key on the server:\n\n```bash\nOPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key\n```\n\nThe adapter reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` at runtime. Do not send this key to the browser.\n\nIf you do not want a server key, see [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok).\n\n## 3. Render the chat\n\n<!-- ::start:framework -->\n\n# React\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-react`. Hold the composer text in `useState`. Pass it to `sendMessage`.\n\n```tsx\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onChange={(event) => setInput(event.target.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n`messages` updates as chunks arrive. `isLoading` is `true` while the run is in flight.\n\nSee the [React API](../api/ai-react).\n\n# Vue\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-vue`. If you are in `<script setup>`, read refs with `.value`. The template unwraps them.\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { ref } from 'vue'\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-vue'\n\nconst input = ref('')\n\nconst { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\n\nfunction handleSubmit() {\n  if (input.value.trim() && !isLoading.value) {\n    sendMessage(input.value)\n    input.value = ''\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <div v-for=\"message in messages\" :key=\"message.id\">\n      <template v-for=\"(part, index) in message.parts\" :key=\"index\">\n        <p v-if=\"part.type === 'text'\">{{ part.content }}</p>\n      </template>\n    </div>\n    <form @submit.prevent=\"handleSubmit\">\n      <input v-model=\"input\" :disabled=\"isLoading\" />\n      <button v-if=\"isLoading\" type=\"button\" @click=\"stop\">Stop</button>\n      <button v-else type=\"submit\" :disabled=\"!input.trim()\">Send</button>\n    </form>\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\nThe composable stops in-flight requests when the component unmounts.\n\nSee the [Vue API](../api/ai-vue).\n\n# Solid\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-solid`. `messages` and `isLoading` are accessors. Call them as functions.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { For, createSignal } from \"solid-js\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-solid\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = createSignal(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      <For each={messages()}>\n        {(message) => (\n          <div>\n            <For each={message.parts}>\n              {(part) =>\n                part.type === \"text\" ? <p>{part.content}</p> : null\n              }\n            </For>\n          </div>\n        )}\n      </For>\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input().trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input());\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input()}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading() ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nSee the [Solid API](../api/ai-solid).\n\n# Svelte\n\nCall `createChat` from `@tanstack/ai-svelte`. The return object uses reactive getters. Read `chat.messages` and `chat.isLoading` with no extra wrapper.\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-svelte'\n\nlet input = $state('')\n\nconst chat = createChat({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n})\n\nfunction handleSubmit() {\n  if (input.trim() && !chat.isLoading) {\n    chat.sendMessage(input)\n    input = ''\n  }\n}\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each chat.messages as message (message.id)}\n    <div>\n      {#each message.parts as part}\n        {#if part.type === 'text'}\n          <p>{part.content}</p>\n        {/if}\n      {/each}\n    </div>\n  {/each}\n\n  <form onsubmit={handleSubmit}>\n    <input bind:value={input} disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n    {#if chat.isLoading}\n      <button type=\"button\" onclick={() => chat.stop()}>Stop</button>\n    {:else}\n      <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!input.trim()}>Send</button>\n    {/if}\n  </form>\n</div>\n```\n\nIf the component can unmount while a response streams, call `chat.stop()` in `onDestroy`.\n\nSee the [Svelte API](../api/ai-svelte).\n\n# Preact\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-preact`. Hold the composer text with `useState` from `preact/hooks`.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from \"preact/hooks\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-preact\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n            part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n          )}\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nSee the [Preact API](../api/ai-preact).\n\n# Angular\n\nCall `injectChat` in a field initializer. State is a `Signal`. Read it by calling the function.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { Component } from \"@angular/core\";\nimport { FormsModule } from \"@angular/forms\";\nimport { injectChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-angular\";\n\n@Component({\n  selector: \"app-chat\",\n  standalone: true,\n  imports: [FormsModule],\n  template: `\n    <div>\n      @for (message of chat.messages(); track message.id) {\n        <div>\n          @for (part of message.parts; track $index) {\n            @if (part.type === \"text\") {\n              <p>{{ part.content }}</p>\n            }\n          }\n        </div>\n      }\n      <form (submit)=\"send($event)\">\n        <input [(ngModel)]=\"draft\" name=\"draft\" [disabled]=\"chat.isLoading()\" />\n        @if (chat.isLoading()) {\n          <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"chat.stop()\">Stop</button>\n        } @else {\n          <button type=\"submit\" [disabled]=\"!draft.trim()\">Send</button>\n        }\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  `,\n})\nexport class ChatComponent {\n  chat = injectChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  draft = \"\";\n\n  send(event: Event) {\n    event.preventDefault();\n    const text = this.draft.trim();\n    if (text && !this.chat.isLoading()) {\n      void this.chat.sendMessage(text);\n      this.draft = \"\";\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCall `injectChat` in a field initializer or the constructor. A call in `ngOnInit` throws.\n\n`injectChat` subscribes to `DestroyRef`. In-flight requests stop when the component is destroyed.\n\nSee the [Angular API](../api/ai-angular).\n\n# Octane\n\nCall `useChat` from `@tanstack/ai-octane`. Hold the composer text in `useState` from `octane`. Octane text controls fire `onInput`.\n\n`@tanstack/ai-octane` publishes uncompiled `.tsrx` source. Add `octane/compiler/vite` (or the rspack / rspeedy equivalent) to the app build.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { useState } from \"octane\";\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-octane\";\n\nexport function Chat() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState(\"\");\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, stop } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  });\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {messages.map((message) => (\n        <div key={message.id}>\n          <p>\n            {message.parts\n              .filter((part) => part.type === \"text\")\n              .map((part) => part.content)\n              .join(\"\")}\n          </p>\n        </div>\n      ))}\n      <form\n        onSubmit={(event) => {\n          event.preventDefault();\n          if (input.trim() === \"\") {\n            return;\n          }\n          void sendMessage(input);\n          setInput(\"\");\n        }}\n      >\n        <input\n          value={input}\n          disabled={isLoading}\n          onInput={(event) => setInput(event.currentTarget.value)}\n        />\n        {isLoading ? (\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={stop}>\n            Stop\n          </button>\n        ) : (\n          <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n        )}\n      </form>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe hook calls `attach()` on mount. It calls `detach()` and `dispose()` on unmount.\n\nSee the [Octane API](../api/ai-octane).\n\n# Remix\n\nCall `createChat(handle, options)` from `@tanstack/ai-remix` inside a `clientEntry` island. Put `connection` and `tools` in setup. They are not serializable `clientEntry` props.\n\n`@tanstack/ai-remix` publishes uncompiled source. Remix compiles JSX through `jsxImportSource` `remix/ui`. Bind the form with the Remix `on` mixin.\n\n```tsx ignore\nimport { createChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-remix\";\nimport { clientEntry, on, type Handle } from \"remix/ui\";\n\nexport const Chat = clientEntry(\n  import.meta.url,\n  function Chat(handle: Handle) {\n    const chat = createChat(handle, {\n      connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n    });\n\n    return () => (\n      <div>\n        {chat.messages.map((message) => (\n          <div key={message.id}>\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n              part.type === \"text\" ? <p key={index}>{part.content}</p> : null,\n            )}\n          </div>\n        ))}\n        <form\n          mix={on(\"submit\", (event) => {\n            event.preventDefault();\n            const form = event.currentTarget;\n            const text = String(\n              new FormData(form).get(\"message\") ?? \"\",\n            ).trim();\n            if (text === \"\") {\n              return;\n            }\n            form.reset();\n            void chat.sendMessage(text);\n          })}\n        >\n          <input name=\"message\" disabled={chat.isLoading} />\n          {chat.isLoading ? (\n            <button type=\"button\" mix={on(\"click\", () => chat.stop())}>\n              Stop\n            </button>\n          ) : (\n            <button type=\"submit\">Send</button>\n          )}\n        </form>\n      </div>\n    );\n  },\n);\n```\n\nRead `chat.messages` and `chat.isLoading` in the render function so each paint sees the latest values.\n\nSee the [Remix API](../api/ai-remix). For a typed headless chat UI, see [Remix Chat UI](../ui/remix).\n\n<!-- ::end:framework -->\n\nSend a message. Tokens show up in the UI.\n\n## Later\n\n- [Tools](../tools/tools) for function calling\n- [Streaming](../chat/streaming) for cancel, callbacks, and transports\n- [Adapters](../adapters/openai) for other providers\n"}
